{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EnhxCt3TsdosNVFyZKzCrX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Stage 2 — Source Snapshot Research\n2\t\n3\tYou are the research stage. Your job is to gather authoritative source material for chapter {{chapter_number}} of {{book_title}} and cache it as dated snapshots that downstream stages can cite without re-fetching.\n4\t\n5\t## Book context\n6\t\n7\t- Exam: {{book_exam_code}} ({{book_exam_authority}})\n8\t- Curriculum version: {{book_curriculum_version}}\n9\t- Book directory: {{book_dir}}\n10\t- Sources must be written to: `{{book_dir}}/sources/`\n11\t\n12\t## Chapter outline (what we need sources for)\n13\t\n14\t{{outline}}\n15\t\n16\t## Your task\n17\t\n18\tFor each exam objective and key concept listed in the outline's `kb_tags`, gather authoritative source material and write it to `{{book_dir}}/sources/` with the naming convention:\n19\t\n20\t```\n21\t{slug}-{YYYY-MM-DD}.md\n22\t```\n23\t\n24\tExamples:\n25\t- `cka-exam-curriculum-{{chapter_number}}-2026-04-18.md`\n26\t- `k8s-docs-namespaces-2026-04-18.md`\n27\t- `pmi-capm-ecow-2026-04-18.md`\n28\t\n29\tEach snapshot file MUST begin with a YAML frontmatter header:\n30\t\n31\t```yaml\n32\t---\n33\tsource_url: \"https://...\"\n34\tfetched_at: \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS-ZZZZ\"\n35\tauthority: \"name of the issuing body\"\n36\tobjectives_covered: [\"1.1\", \"1.2\"]\n37\tconcepts_covered: [\"...\"]\n38\t---\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\tFollowed by the verbatim relevant content from the source, lightly trimmed to stay on-topic. Do not paraphrase — downstream audits verify facts against this exact text.\n42\t\n43\t### Priority order for sources\n44\t\n45\t1. **Official exam authority pages** (PMI, CompTIA, ISC2, Linux Foundation, etc.) — exam objectives, exam format, eligibility\n46\t2. **Official vendor documentation** (kubernetes.io/docs, PMBOK, etc.) — technical truth\n47\t3. **Official supplementary** (RFCs, NIST SPs, ISO standards cited by exam) — deep technical references\n48\t4. **NOT acceptable**: third-party tutorials, blog posts, exam dump sites, unofficial summaries\n49\t\n50\t### Produce `research-manifest.md` at `{{chapter_dir}}/research-manifest.md`\n51\t\n52\tStructure:\n53\t\n54\t```markdown\n55\t# Research Manifest — {{book_exam_code}} Chapter {{chapter_number}}\n56\t\n57\t## Snapshots fetched\n58\t\n59\t| Snapshot | Authority | Objectives | Concepts |\n60\t|---|---|---|---|\n61\t| cka-exam-curriculum-1-2026-04-18.md | Linux Foundation | 1.1, 1.2 | cluster-architecture |\n62\t| ... |\n63\t\n64\t## Gaps\n65\t\n66\tAny objective/concept in the outline that you could NOT find an authoritative source for. Flag these clearly — the drafting stage must NOT make up facts to fill them.\n67\t\n68\t## Notes for the author\n69\t\n70\tAnything ambiguous in the sources, version mismatches, or places where sources disagree.\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\t## Constraints\n74\t\n75\t- NEVER invent source URLs. If you cannot find an authoritative source, list the gap.\n76\t- NEVER write facts to snapshots that don't appear in the source. The snapshot is verbatim evidence.\n77\t- Date every filename. Undated snapshots are drift risk.\n78\t- Prefer the exam authority's own page over vendor docs when they conflict on an exam-relevant detail (the exam tests what the authority says, not what the vendor says).\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccf3f627-6476-4f00-aaf5-561fbd0f1a2c","uuid":"3d5e405c-51ca-4533-8275-703bb1a53433","timestamp":"2026-08-24T07:09:07.809Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\pipeline\\prompts\\02_research_snapshot.md","content":"# Stage 2 — Source Snapshot Research\n\nYou are the research stage. Your job is to gather authoritative source material for chapter {{chapter_number}} of {{book_title}} and cache it as dated snapshots that downstream stages can cite without re-fetching.\n\n## Book context\n\n- Exam: {{book_exam_code}} ({{book_exam_authority}})\n- Curriculum version: {{book_curriculum_version}}\n- Book directory: {{book_dir}}\n- Sources must be written to: `{{book_dir}}/sources/`\n\n## Chapter outline (what we need sources for)\n\n{{outline}}\n\n## Your task\n\nFor each exam objective and key concept listed in the outline's `kb_tags`, gather authoritative source material and write it to `{{book_dir}}/sources/` with the naming convention:\n\n```\n{slug}-{YYYY-MM-DD}.md\n```\n\nExamples:\n- `cka-exam-curriculum-{{chapter_number}}-2026-04-18.md`\n- `k8s-docs-namespaces-2026-04-18.md`\n- `pmi-capm-ecow-2026-04-18.md`\n\nEach snapshot file MUST begin with a YAML frontmatter header:\n\n```yaml\n---\nsource_url: \"https://...\"\nfetched_at: \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS-ZZZZ\"\nauthority: \"name of the issuing body\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"1.1\", \"1.2\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"...\"]\n---\n```\n\nFollowed by the verbatim relevant content from the source, lightly trimmed to stay on-topic. Do not paraphrase — downstream audits verify facts against this exact text.\n\n### Priority order for sources\n\n1. **Official exam authority pages** (PMI, CompTIA, ISC2, Linux Foundation, etc.) — exam objectives, exam format, eligibility\n2. **Official vendor documentation** (kubernetes.io/docs, PMBOK, etc.) — technical truth\n3. **Official supplementary** (RFCs, NIST SPs, ISO standards cited by exam) — deep technical references\n4. **NOT acceptable**: third-party tutorials, blog posts, exam dump sites, unofficial summaries\n\n### Produce `research-manifest.md` at `{{chapter_dir}}/research-manifest.md`\n\nStructure:\n\n```markdown\n# Research Manifest — {{book_exam_code}} Chapter {{chapter_number}}\n\n## Snapshots fetched\n\n| Snapshot | Authority | Objectives | Concepts |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| cka-exam-curriculum-1-2026-04-18.md | Linux Foundation | 1.1, 1.2 | cluster-architecture |\n| ... |\n\n## Gaps\n\nAny objective/concept in the outline that you could NOT find an authoritative source for. Flag these clearly — the drafting stage must NOT make up facts to fill them.\n\n## Notes for the author\n\nAnything ambiguous in the sources, version mismatches, or places where sources disagree.\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- NEVER invent source URLs. If you cannot find an authoritative source, list the gap.\n- NEVER write facts to snapshots that don't appear in the source. The snapshot is verbatim evidence.\n- Date every filename. Undated snapshots are drift risk.\n- Prefer the exam authority's own page over vendor docs when they conflict on an exam-relevant detail (the exam tests what the authority says, not what the vendor says).\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}}}
